# M6. Losing the last handle control mid-motion stops and holds (hand_controls_lost), and outside bench mode
# nothing starts without one. A handle's hello or loss also withdraws a pending Confirm target.
expect motion mode ready
key torque-on-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque left on
key pose-ready-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion command arm.go_to_pose started operator_cli
wait 200
key hand-unplug
expect motion fault hand_controls_lost system
expect motion command arm.go_to_pose faulted operator_cli
wait 200
key inspect-hold-left
expect sim left follower hold ok
absent 1000 sim goal-write left follower
# The hold read the arm first: each goal is where the arm was at the stop, within 0.5°.
key inspect-hold-tight-left
expect sim left follower hold tight ok
# The cause is still there.
key operator-clear
expect motion command fault.clear refused:cause_present operator_cli
key hand-unplug
expect module hand-right-sim ok
# It says hello twice (at boot and to the Pi's hello.request); each hello would withdraw a pending target.
wait 500
key operator-clear
wait 2100
key c
expect motion cleared all faults
# A pending target is withdrawn when the handle goes away.
key pose-handover-left
expect motion target arm.go_to_pose operator_cli
key hand-unplug
expect motion target-ended withdrawn: hand control lost
# Idle with no handle: a move is refused before anyone is asked to press Confirm.
key pose-handover-left
expect motion command arm.go_to_pose refused:no_hand_control operator_cli
key q
